Intro F A 7 Dm 7 Bb 7 C 7 F 7 C+ 7(#9)

{comment: Chorus}
Bb 7 F 7
Somebody give Him some praise, somebody lift your voice
C 7 F 7 F 7 /A
Somebody testify and tell us of the good He’s done
Bb 7 F 7
Make a joyful noise and sing, let the rafters ring
C 7 F 7
For the rest of your days, for all His marvelous ways, somebody give Him some praise
Verses 1 & 2
Bb 7 F 7
1. You may feel underserving, I know sometimes I do
2. “Let everything that hath breath,” that’s what the Bible says
Bb 7 F 7
1. But by His blood, we’re worthy to give the praise He’s due.
2. No matter who you are, you are more than blessed
Bb 7 F 7
1. You don’t have to be perfect, you just need to be forgiven.
2. Offer up some praises, and give Him glory, too
G 7 C+ 7(#9)
1. He’s given you a chance to live a life worth living.
2. He deserves it all for all He’s done for you

